cppgm is an independently maintained adaptation. Its authors have
substantially edited, consolidated, renumbered and extended the original
course into 37 assignments. The compiler implementation, reference tools,
regenerated outputs and current teaching sequence are maintained by this
project. Current PA numbers do not correspond to original CPPGM numbering.

Questions about inherited material should be directed to the repository
maintainers.

The WebAssembly reference material under doc/wasm/ retains its upstream
authorship and license notices. The tool conventions use the Artistic
License 2.0; the core specification documents use the W3C Software and
Document Notice and License. Source revisions and hashes are recorded in
doc/wasm/manifest.json.

The bare WebAssembly C library supplement incorporates musl string objects
from WASI SDK 34.0 (wasi-libc revision 2e6fb9d8ee0c) at build time. The
upstream wasi-libc license texts and musl copyright notice are retained in
dev/runtime/wasm-freestanding/licenses and installed beside the archive.
The hosted WASI C23 stdio supplement adapts the formatting engines and
stream adapters from the same wasi-libc revision. Its build installs the
same license texts and copyright notice.
The hosted WASI C23 math supplement also incorporates CORE-MATH sources
under the MIT license. The individual copyright notices and license text
are retained in third_party/core-math and installed with the runtime archive.
The WASI binary128 `log1pl` implementation adapts FreeBSD's msun under the
BSD 2-Clause License. Its copyright and license notice are retained in
dev/runtime/wasi-c23/licenses and installed with the runtime archive.
The WASI C23 narrowing operations incorporate Berkeley SoftFloat under the
BSD 3-Clause License. Its notices are retained in third_party/softfloat and
installed with the runtime archive.

